.TH GIBSON-UI 1 "August 2026" "GIBSON 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gibson-ui \- travel through the file system as a cinematic city
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gibson-ui
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ directory ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
GIBSON is a native Wayland file-system visualiser.
It contains a Bash terminal and a file navigator.
Directory changes move the camera through a city of directory towers.
.PP
GIBSON uses the Omarchy palette and background when they are available.
Wallpaper mode aligns the image with its position on the current monitor.
It uses a built-in palette on other Wayland systems.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --root
Start at the top-level directory.
.TP
.B --fullscreen
Start in borderless fullscreen mode.
.TP
.B --cockpit
Move to an empty Hyprland workspace and start in fullscreen mode.
On other compositors, this option starts in fullscreen mode only.
.TP
.BI --fps " NUMBER"
Set the application limit to 30, 60, or 120 frames per second.
.TP
.B --uncapped
Remove the application frame limit.
.TP
.B --perf
Write renderer statistics to the application log every two seconds.
On supported GPUs, also sample GPU pass times without waiting for the GPU.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show command help.
.TP
.B -V, --version
Show the version.
.SH CONTROLS
.TP
.B F2
Change between terminal and file-navigator control.
.TP
.B F3
Show or hide the terminal pane.
.TP
.B F4
Show or hide the file navigator.
.TP
.B F10
Open or close settings.
.TP
.B F11
Change the fullscreen state.
.TP
.B Left, Right, R
Orbit left, orbit right, or reset the orbit.
.TP
.B Up, Down, Page Up, Page Down, Home, End
Move through the file navigator.
.TP
.B Enter
Enter a directory or open a file with the default application.
.TP
.B Backspace
Move to the parent directory.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/gibson/gibson.toml
User settings.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/omarchy/current/theme/colors.toml
Optional live Omarchy palette.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/omarchy/current/background
Optional live Omarchy background.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bash (1),
.BR foot (1),
.BR hyprctl (1),
.BR xdg-open (1)
